I walk forward in the market.
There is a fruit cart there.
There are yellow bananas on the cart.
There is a small board there.
The price is written on the board.
The price of one dozen bananas is eighty rupees.
I stop near the fruit cart.
The vendor is a young man.
I say, "Bhaiya, I want half a dozen bananas."
He says, "Okay, madam."
He puts six bananas in my bag.
The price of half a dozen bananas is forty rupees.
I have a five-hundred rupee note.
I give that large note to him.
I wait there.
He counts out the remaining rupees.
He gives those rupees to me.
I say thank you to him.
